From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:42:10 -0700
Subject: Prevent sourceURL annotations from spoofing origins and being locally
 overridden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scripts can specify sourceURL annotations and source maps that are fully controlled by the page. This change ensures that:
- HTTP and HTTPS sourceURL annotations must match the origin of the script frame to prevent cross-origin resource spoofing.
- sourceURL annotations cannot evict existing UISourceCodes fetched directly from the network.
- UISourceCodes generated from sourceURL annotations or source maps cannot be saved as local overrides, preventing override directory poisoning.

Bug: 553931271
Change-Id: Ib9ac1c265445980585706830385697ee6d6d29d1
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8421102
Commit-Queue: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Simon Zünd <szuend@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0e5527264722c85d3771c38762ce63e9485dc165)

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
This branch has no SDK.SecurityOrigin class or Target.inspectedSecurityOrigin(), and ResourceTreeFrame.securityOrigin is a getter returning string|null, so #isTrustworthySourceURL() compares serialized origin strings (ParsedURL.extractOrigin, lowercased as upstream does) and still rejects the annotation when no origin can be established.

